  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Major release: combines the Android 10.1.2 + iOS 5.72.0 SDK updates with cross-platform consistency fixes.\n\nNEW\n- GetStorefrontCountryCode() — exposes the user's App Store / Play Store ISO 3166-1 country (e.g. \"US\", \"CZ\"), independent of CultureInfo.CurrentCulture.\n- Unified GetPriceFor(PriceDuration) / GetPriceWithCurrencyFor(PriceDuration) — supports Daily / Weekly / Monthly / Yearly; replaces the separate Monthly/Weekly helpers.\n- StoreType: RcBilling / External / Paddle / TestStore / Galaxy members are now mapped on both iOS and Android.\n\nFIXED\n- #103 PriceLocalized formatting is now deterministic across runs (was: same currency formatted three different ways on the same device). Whole-number prices drop the trailing \",00\".\n- #106 PurchaseErrorStatus mapping now uses explicit per-platform tables — Android codes were silently mis-cast to wrong wrapper members (e.g. CustomerInfoError, SignatureVerificationFailed). Raised matching upstream issues at RevenueCat/purchases-android#3469 and RevenueCat/purchases-ios#6777.\n- #81 / #37 ProductDto.SubscriptionPeriod is now a proper SubscriptionPeriodDto { Value, Unit } — was a meaningless NSObject hex string on iOS.\n\nBREAKING\n- Android: minimum API raised from 21 to 23.\n- ProductDto.SubscriptionPeriod: string → SubscriptionPeriodDto?\n- PricingDto: removed PriceLocalizedPerMonth / PriceLocalizedPerWeek. Use GetPriceWithCurrencyFor(PriceDuration.Monthly/Weekly) instead.\n- Removed GetMonthlyPrice / GetWeeklyPrice / GetMonthlyPriceWithCurrency / GetWeeklyPriceWithCurrency — use GetPriceFor / GetPriceWithCurrencyFor with the PriceDuration enum.\n- IRevenueCatBilling has a new method GetStorefrontCountryCode (binary-breaking for implementers; transparent for callers).",
